### CRUD API Examples
### You can use this file with VS Code REST Client extension or similar tools

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@apiUrl = {{baseUrl}}/api/resources
@apiKey = test-api-key-12345

### Health Check (No authentication required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Create a new resource
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "Laptop",
  "description": "High-performance laptop",
  "category": "electronics",
  "status": "active"
}

### Create another resource
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "TypeScript Handbook",
  "description": "Learn TypeScript from scratch",
  "category": "books",
  "status": "active"
}

### Create resource with minimal data
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "Wireless Mouse"
}

### List all resources
GET {{apiUrl}}
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### List resources with filters - by category
GET {{apiUrl}}?category=electronics
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### List resources with filters - by name (partial match)
GET {{apiUrl}}?name=Type
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### List resources with filters - by status
GET {{apiUrl}}?status=active
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### List resources with pagination
GET {{apiUrl}}?limit=10&offset=0
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Combined filters
GET {{apiUrl}}?category=electronics&status=active&limit=5
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Get resource by ID (change ID to actual ID)
GET {{apiUrl}}/1
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Update resource (change ID to actual ID)
PUT {{apiUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "Updated Laptop",
  "description": "Ultra high-performance laptop",
  "status": "inactive"
}

### Partial update - only status
PUT {{apiUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "status": "archived"
}

### Delete resource (change ID to actual ID)
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/1
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Error Examples

### Error: Missing API key
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "This will fail without API key"
}

### Error: Invalid API key
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: wrong-api-key

{
  "name": "This will fail with wrong API key"
}

### Error: Missing required field (name)
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "description": "This will fail"
}

### Error: Invalid status value
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "Test",
  "status": "invalid-status"
}

### Error: Empty name
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": ""
}

### Error: Name too long (>255 chars)
POST {{apiUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
}

### Error: Resource not found
GET {{apiUrl}}/99999
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Error: Invalid resource ID
GET {{apiUrl}}/invalid
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Error: Update with no fields
PUT {{apiUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{}
